From c3ba681c61689b42b7513184a41534c1bbf1e8c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dlgpdmsly2 <dlgpdmsly2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:10:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Restore selection range on docs undo/redo, not just the
 caret

Undo restored the caret but collapsed the selection: the docs Yorkie store recorded only activeCursorPos (never activeSelection) in the undo-history presence set, and the editor's undoFn/redoFn only moved the caret.

Record activeSelection alongside activeCursorPos via a shared recordHistoryPresence helper (21 sites), flush the pre-edit selection into presence synchronously in setCursorForHistory so Yorkie's reverse captures it, add getPresenceSelection, and re-apply the restored range via selection.setRange in undo/redo. activeSelection defaults to a concrete collapsed range so the presence key is always tracked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
