From b7780e36b9ae7c70786598f901e4cb0cdae1ea2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dlgpdmsly2 <dlgpdmsly2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:24:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Record selection in toolbar style path so undo restores
 it

applyStyleImpl (toolbar/Cmd-B) bypasses the text-editor saveSnapshot hook, so it recorded no reversible caret/selection presence - undo after formatting collapsed the selection. It now calls setCursorForHistory(cursor.position, selection.range) before doc.applyInlineStyle.

Also harden restoreSelectionFromPresence: validate both anchor and focus blocks (not just the table-cell blockId) and clamp both endpoints for table selections too. Add an editor-level regression test driving applyStyle + undo through the public EditorAPI with YorkieDocStore.

